2FA email OTP resend verification - 2026-08-11 CST

BASELINE
- Registration OTP already retried/resend up to 3 times in protocol, Roxy, and Cloak paths.
- The 2FA re-authentication path sent one email OTP, waited once, and validated once.
- A delayed, missing, expired, or reused 2FA re-authentication OTP ended the 2FA setup.

MODIFIED BEHAVIOR
- Protocol and fingerprint-browser 2FA re-authentication now use up to 3 OTP attempts.
- Mailbox wait failure triggers the email-otp/send endpoint before the next wait.
- HTTP 401 or explicit invalid/expired OTP responses trigger resend and retry.
- The registration OTP and each rejected OTP are excluded from later mailbox polling.
- Protocol and browser paths emit distinct resend/attempt logs.

